LANGUAGE English

BOOK Halls ORDERED NO KEEP LOOP

	PAGE ExploreHall1
		TRIGGERED BY @ExploreHall1
		
		PROLOG """
			The door has a dirty push plate. When you push on it, you discover
			it's locked. An investigator with the {c:QItemBrassKey} can open
			this door.
		"""
		BUTTON "Explore"
		
		TEXT """
			When you open the door, the rush of cold, stale air sends a chill
			down your spine.

			You stop for a moment and look back down at the footsteps leading
			to this door. You wonder how the air feels so stale if this door
			has been opened recently.
		"""
	
		$mythosHall = TRUE
		exploredHall1 = TRUE AFTER


		exploredHall1 = TRUE AFTER
	END ExploreHall1

	PAGE PlaceHall1
		TEXT """
			You look through the doorway to find a hall. It is clear that it
			was intended for the servants:  plain and dark. Place the
			{c:TileHall1} tile, a door, and a wall as indicated.
			
			Move one space space into the hall.
		"""
						
		REMOVE TokenExploreHallway1ViaDiningRoom
		
		ADD TileHall1, TokenDoorHall1, TokenWallHall1
	END PlaceHall1
	
	PAGE PlaceHall1Gallery
		TEXT """
			To your immediate right is a door. Place an Explore token as
			indicated.
		"""
		
		ADD TokenExploreGalleryViaHall1
	END PlaceHall1Gallery
	
	PAGE PlaceHall1Painting
		TEXT """
			On the left, a painting glows with unnatural
			light. You can almost feel it calling to you. You shake it off
			because paintings don't have power. Place a Search token as 
			indicated.
			
			As you look away, you catch something moving in your 
			peripheral vision. You glance back and the painting is still
			lightly glowing, something that suddently seems more troubling.
		"""
		
		ADD TokenSearchHall1Picture
	END PlaceHall1Painting
	
	PAGE PlaceHall1Evidence
		TEXT """
			You look down. The rug on the floor is old and beautiful, if
			dirty and poorly cared for. One corner is folded up and looks
			like it has been that way for years. You should probably put
			it back so you don't trip over it.
			
			Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
		
		ADD TokenSearchHall1Rug
	END PlaceHall1Evidence
	
	PAGE PlaceHall1Sight
		TEXT """
			The hall stretches forward. Place a Sight token as indicated.
			
			As you look around, something doesn't feel right.
			You feel like you are being watched.
		"""
		
		ADD TokenSightHall2ViaHall1
		
		IF foundJournal THEN EXIT
	END PlaceHall1Sight
	
	PAGE PlaceHall1Journal
		TEXT """
			<i>The book on the floor,</i> you remind yourself. You turn 
			around and step back. Move one space into the {c:TileDiningRoom}.
			
			You look over, see the book, and bend down to pick it up. Gain
			the {c:QItemJournal} unique item.
			
			You look at the book you picked up:  small, thin, and
			leather-bound. You flip through the pages: 	it's a journal.
			The first entry was scrawled last Sunday.

			Maybe you should hold onto it to give back to Benjamin when you
			see him later today. And maybe take a quick look.

			Gain the {c:QItemJournal} Unique Item, then remove it's
			Search token. An investigator holding the {c:QItemJournal}
			can interact with it in the app.
		"""
		
		REMOVE TokenSearchDiningRoomJournal
		foundJournal = TRUE
		
		EXIT
	END PlaceHall1Journal
END Hallway